     "type": "intro",
     "title": "An Emperor Wrote a Diary to Himself",
     "content": "Imagine the most powerful man in the world — ruler of 60 million people, commander of legions, master of an empire stretching from Britain to Syria — and at the end of each day, by candlelight in a war tent on the Danube frontier, he picks up a stylus and writes notes to **himself**. Not for publication. Not for posterity. Just reminders, in Greek, to be a better person tomorrow.\n\nThat man was **Marcus Aurelius** (121-180 CE), and those private notes became the **Meditations** — the most influential ethical document ever written by a head of state. He never titled it, never edited it, never intended you to read it.\n\nBut you will. And it will change how you think about every difficulty you face.",
