     "type": "visual",
     "title": "From Slave to Emperor",
     "content": "Notice the **paradox of Stoicism's transmission**: its most influential teacher was a slave (Epictetus), and his most devoted reader was an emperor (Marcus). The philosophy taught both that **external station is morally irrelevant** — only your reasoning and choices matter.",
