     "explanation": "Stoicism was founded around 301 BCE by Zeno of Citium (a city on Cyprus) after he was shipwrecked near Athens. He taught from the Stoa Poikile, the \"Painted Porch\" in the Athenian Agora. The Greek word stoa simply means porch or colonnade — so \"Stoicism\" literally means \"the porch school.\" Marcus and Epictetus came centuries later. Socrates predated Stoicism by ~100 years but was a major influence on Zeno.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Origins of Stoicism</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"180\" width=\"800\" height=\"280\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"235\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">THE STOA POIKILE</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"285\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">\"Painted Porch\" in Athens</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"325\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">A colonnade in the Agora decorated with frescoes</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"365\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Zeno taught there free, publicly, ~301 BCE</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"410\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">stoa = porch → \"Stoicism\"</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"500\" width=\"800\" height=\"220\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"555\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">ZENO OF CITIUM</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"605\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Phoenician merchant, shipwrecked near Athens</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"645\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Studied with Crates the Cynic, then founded his own school</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"680\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">\"I made a prosperous voyage when I was shipwrecked\"</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"760\" width=\"800\" height=\"280\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"815\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">THE LINEAGE</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"865\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Zeno → Cleanthes → Chrysippus → Seneca → Epictetus → Marcus</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"910\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">From Athens (4th c BCE) to Rome (2nd c CE)</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"950\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Five centuries of refinement</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"990\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Marcus was the lineage's last great voice</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Stoicism's origin point"
     }
