     "explanation": "Every word of the definition is load-bearing. BRIEF and SCHEDULED distinguish it from rumination, which is open-ended and intrusive. DELIBERATE means you choose the time and scenario — the rehearsal happens in a venue you control. SPECIFIC converts vague dread into a nameable problem that planning can address. And RESPONDING WELL is the most-forgotten component: you don't just visualize the storm, you visualize yourself sailing it — examining the criticism for truth, executing the backup plan, bearing the loss with composure. The practice makes no prediction that bad things WILL happen (that's pessimism) and involves no magical bargaining. Cicero's formula captures the goal: foresight softens arrival. The Stoic expects the best, prepares for the worst, and is surprised by neither.",
