     "explanation": "Maya's session checks every box of the rehearsal column: she chose the time (scheduled), it has a hard stop (bounded), it targets one named event (specific), the protagonist is her own competent response (agentive), and it terminates in an artifact — a backup answer (conclusive). Leo's nights check every box of the rumination column: intrusive, open-ended, escalating in vagueness ('everything collapses'), starring the catastrophe with himself as passive victim, ending only when exhaustion intervenes. The volume of his worrying isn't thoroughness — repetition without structure sensitizes rather than habituates, deepening the groove each loop. Note also that physical drills (Seneca's option) are a powerful supplement but not a requirement; Marcus's 2.1 morning rehearsal is purely mental and fully counts. The dividing line is never the imagery — both imagine failure — it's the machinery: who chose it, where it stops, and what it produces.",
