     "type": "practice",
     "title": "Practice: The Thirty-Second Subtraction",
     "content": "**The smallest premeditatio — a daily gratitude engine you can run anywhere. Start tonight.**\n\n**THE CORE DRILL (30 seconds, once a day):**\n\n1. **Pick one thing you used today without noticing.** Rotate categories through the week:\n   • Mon — a **person** (partner, friend, the colleague who covers for you)\n   • Tue — a **faculty** (sight, hearing, walking, memory)\n   • Wed — an **object** (your bed, hot water, glasses, phone)\n   • Thu — a **circumstance** (peace where you live, employment, health)\n   • Fri — a **pleasure** (coffee, music, the evening walk)\n   • Sat — an **institution** (clean water systems, libraries, medicine)\n   • Sun — **free choice**\n\n2. **Run the subtraction, vividly, for 30 seconds.** Not the abstract thought \"it could be gone\" — the concrete scene: the chair empty, the silence where the voice was, the cold tap. Let it actually sting for a breath. The sting is the mechanism engaging.\n\n3. **Return and notice.** Open your eyes to a world where the thing exists. Marcus's phrasing (7.27): reflect *how eagerly it would be sought* if absent — and observe that you have, without seeking, what the seeker wants.\n\n4. **One-line log.** Write the item and one word for what came back. (\"Hot water — luxury.\") The log matters: paging back through three weeks of entries is itself a potent dose.\n\n**RULES:**\n• **One item, once a day.** More is not better — overuse flattens the effect (the subtraction itself can hedonically adapt).\n• **Never run it on a current acute loss or fear** — this drill is for the invisible goods, not open wounds.\n• **End on the return**, always. The exercise is complete when the thing has been restored to perception, not when the sadness peaks.\n\nThis is the practice Irvine calls the single highest-yield technique in Stoicism: **thirty seconds of imagined winter to make the actual day feel like spring.**",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">THE 30-SECOND SUBTRACTION</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Daily gratitude engine</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"180\" width=\"800\" height=\"240\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"230\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">WEEKLY ROTATION</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"275\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">Mon: person — Tue: faculty — Wed: object</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"310\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">Thu: circumstance — Fri: pleasure</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"345\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">Sat: institution — Sun: free choice</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"390\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">One thing you used today without noticing</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"450\" width=\"800\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"498\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">SUBTRACT — VIVIDLY, 30 SECONDS</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"535\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">The chair empty. The silence. The cold tap.</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"572\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Let it sting for a breath — the sting is the mechanism</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"640\" width=\"800\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"688\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">RETURN AND LOG</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"725\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Notice you have what the seeker wants (7.27)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"762\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">One line: \"Hot water — luxury\"</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"830\" width=\"800\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.12)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"878\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">RULES</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"915\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">Once daily — overuse flattens the effect</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"948\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">Never on an open wound. Always end on the return.</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"1020\" width=\"700\" height=\"50\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"1053\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"19\">Thirty seconds of imagined winter → the day feels like spring</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Imagined winter, actual spring"
     }
